    "title": "Liv Morgan's Defenseless Title Reign Adressed By Roxanne Perez - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Thomas Lowson ,\n51 minutes ago\nLiv Morgan captured the WWE Women’s World Championship at WWE WrestleMania 42, but her reign has left many fans feeling underwhelmed.\nSince dethroning Stephanie Vaquer on April 20, Morgan has competed just once, defeating Sol Ruca on the post-WrestleMania RAW in non-title action.\nOn a recent edition of the “Complex Graps Wrestling” podcast, Roxanne Perez was asked about Morgan’s title reign and addressed the lack of matches. She said,\nREAD MORE: Bully Ray Blasts Oba Femi, John Cena Explains Shift From WWE To Hollywood, Rhea Ripley/Jacob Fatu\nREAD MORE: Jade Cargill Says She Gets Paid By The Match, Jey Uso Tells Fans To ‘Chill’ After Backlash\n“I think Liv Morgan is doing a fantastic job at being the Women’s World Champion. I’m a little confused as to why people don’t want to challenge her for her title. Um, I don’t know, people are scared, or what the deal is.”\nPerez was also asked what her reign as WWE Women’s World Champion woul look like if she was to win the gold. She said,\n“I think that any one of us would hold the title differently, but I also think that we would stand as a unit, and, you know, have the numbers game in our favor, regardless of the champion.”\nPerez is a two-time WWE NXT Women’s Champion, a former WWE NXT Women’s Tag Team Champion, and a former WWE Women’s Tag Team Champion.\n1",
